# Stickers hub: why some product images look relatively smaller (learned 2026-09-25)

## Symptom

On `/stickers`, **some** product images look smaller than neighbours after `h-56` + contain. Confirmed SKUs include:

- **Basic / Premium sheets:** Cute Animal Friends Name label, Wise Owl Extra-Large Name label, 9-Color Pastel Pearl Name Label, Premium Holographic Name label, …
- **Stationery Essentials** (also subject padding — `stationery-essentials-image-size.mdc`)
- **Mixed Labels** tall sheets

**Square** uploads (Happy Bear 500×500, some Mixed 1024×1024) look **larger** in the same card.

## Why (not a per-SKU CSS bug)

Hub: same `imageLayout="full"` → `h-56` + `object-contain` + `inset-1`. Contain keeps full art; landscape shell + **portrait file** → narrow centered column + gray sides.

Live fit estimate (laptop ~4-col, inner ~272×216):

| SKU | File | AR | Drawn | Area fill |
|-----|------|-----|-------|-----------|
| Cute Animal Friends | 864×1184 | 0.73 | ~158×216 | ~58% |
| Wise Owl Extra-Large | 864×1184 | 0.73 | ~158×216 | ~58% |
| 9-Color Pastel Pearl | 896×1195 | 0.75 | ~162×216 | ~60% |
| Happy Bear (square) | 500×500 | 1.0 | ~216×216 | ~79% |
| Holographic Mixed (square) | 1024×1024 | 1.0 | ~216×216 | ~79% |

Most **name-label sheet mockups** are ~3:4 portrait PNGs — that is why those Basics/Premiums look “small” next to square assets. Laptop worse: more columns → narrower cards.

Related: badges look oversized on the same cards (`product-card-merch-badges.mdc`).

## How to fix — does admin need to re-upload?

**Short answer:**  
- **Must re-make / re-upload?** Only if the goal is **equal visual fill** while **keeping full sheet visible** (`object-contain`). Then yes: export nearer-**square** (or less empty margin) listing images and replace in Admin → Products.  
- **Code-only “make all fill the box”?** Possible with `object-cover`, but **do not** — crops sticker sheets (owner already rejected that zoom look).  
- **Optional small code tweaks** (`h-60`, fewer laptop columns): make **all** cards a bit larger; portrait SKUs stay **relatively** smaller than square ones. Does **not** remove the gap without new assets.

### Recommended path (ops)

1. Keep storefront **contain** (full artwork).
2. For listing/primary image, prefer **~1:1** (e.g. 1000×1000) or soft pad the portrait sheet onto a square canvas (sheet centered, light/white/gray margins **in the file** so contain fills the hub shell).
3. Re-upload that file as the product image (and gallery lead if used).
4. Stationery: tighter crop of the product (less empty margin in the photo).

Admin does **not** need to redesign the physical sticker — only the **catalog listing image canvas**.

### If owner declines re-upload

Accept letterboxing, or only bump shell/grid slightly — document that relative size difference remains.

## Ways to make them “the same size”

| Approach | Same what? | Admin re-upload? | Tradeoff |
|----------|------------|------------------|----------|
| **A. Keep contain** (current) | Same outer box | No | Drawn size still varies |
| **B. `object-cover`** | Fills box | No | Crops — **avoid** |
| **D. Normalize uploads** (preferred for parity) | Art fills similarly under contain | **Yes** (square / padded canvas) | Best quality |
| **E. Taller shell** | Slightly wider portrait | No | Relative gap remains |
| **F. Fewer desktop columns** | All larger in px | No | Relative gap remains |

**Default:** keep **A** until owner wants parity → then **D** (re-upload), not cover.

## Do not

- Treat Cute Animal / Wise Owl / Pastel Pearl as special broken CSS — they share the portrait+contain class
- Tell admin “rebuild the whole product” — only **listing image canvas**
- Per-product scale hacks in `ProductCard`
- Switch hub stickers to `object-cover` to fake equal fill
